00:59:09.131 --> 00:59:10.164
Take this.

1254
00:59:10.266 --> 00:59:12.766
Take this. Put it back.

1255
00:59:22.875 --> 00:59:25.314
If anything happens.
you take this.

1256
00:59:25.416 --> 00:59:27.379
and you stab him
in the neck as hard

1257
00:59:27.481 --> 00:59:28.613
and as fast as you can.

1258
00:59:28.715 --> 00:59:29.910
- No! No. no!
- It has to be you.

1259
00:59:30.012 --> 00:59:31.178
He's watching me too closely.

1260
00:59:31.280 --> 00:59:33.551
- He won't expect us to do it.
- Sister. no!

1261
00:59:33.653 --> 00:59:35.055
Okay. Let's have a code word.

1262
00:59:35.157 --> 00:59:36.390
Okay? Um...

1263
00:59:36.492 --> 00:59:38.357
Hey. if I say
"magic underwear."

1264
00:59:38.459 --> 00:59:40.288
that means stab. Okay?

1265
00:59:41.064 --> 00:59:42.062
(DISTANT THUD)

1266
00:59:42.164 --> 00:59:43.894
He's coming.

1267
00:59:43.996 --> 00:59:46.595
Magic underwear.
That's the code word. Okay?

1268
00:59:46.697 --> 00:59:47.867
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1269
00:59:50.403 --> 00:59:52.069
(CREAKING)

1270
00:59:53.077 --> 00:59:54.335
(PAXTON WHIMPERS)

1271
00:59:55.276 --> 00:59:57.008
(DOOR UNLOCKS)

1272
01:00:02.613 --> 01:00:03.577
(DOOR OPENS)

1273
01:00:03.680 --> 01:00:05.885
(CREAKING)

1274
01:00:07.916 --> 01:00:10.318
(CREAKING CONTINUES)

1275
01:00:16.260 --> 01:00:18.493
- (OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)
- (BOTH BREATHING HEAVILY)

1276
01:00:18.595 --> 01:00:19.800
Mr. Reed?

1277
01:00:20.668 --> 01:00:22.902
(OMINOUS MUSIC
CONTINUES PLAYING)

1278
01:00:25.274 --> 01:00:27.676
(SQUELCHY FOOTSTEPS)

1279
01:00:29.806 --> 01:00:31.878
(LANTERN CREAKING)

1280
01:00:34.813 --> 01:00:36.949
- (WHIMPERS)
- Mrs. Reed?

1281
01:00:38.616 --> 01:00:39.919
Is that you?

1282
01:00:44.494 --> 01:00:46.255
(OMINOUS MUSIC
CONTINUES PLAYING)

1283
01:00:54.699 --> 01:00:56.903
(PAXTON WHIMPERING)

1284
01:00:58.836 --> 01:01:00.107
(BARNES INHALES SHARPLY)

1285
01:01:00.209 --> 01:01:01.204
(PAXTON GASPS)

1286
01:01:03.410 --> 01:01:05.373
(BONES CRACKING)

1287
01:01:12.685 --> 01:01:14.349
What's happening to her?

1288
01:01:15.223 --> 01:01:16.852
(RATTLE)

1289
01:01:16.955 --> 01:01:19.123
<i>(CREEP</i> BY RADIOHEAD PLAYING)

1290
01:01:25.567 --> 01:01:26.498
(MR. REED MOCKINGLY SINGING)

1291
01:01:26.600 --> 01:01:27.802
<i>♪ But I'm a creep ♪</i>

1292
01:01:28.469 --> 01:01:30.633
<i>♪ I'm a weirdo ♪</i>

1293
01:01:30.735 --> 01:01:31.832
(MR. REED LAUGHING)

1294
01:01:31.934 --> 01:01:33.368
BARNES: Mr. Reed?

1295
01:01:36.577 --> 01:01:37.812
BARNES: Where are you?

1296
01:01:37.914 --> 01:01:40.078
- (BARNES BREATHING HEAVILY)
- (MR. REED HUMS ALONG)

1297
01:01:43.180 --> 01:01:45.314
<i>♪ Couldn't look you
in the eye ♪</i>

1298
01:01:48.789 --> 01:01:51.155
<i>♪ You're just like an angel ♪</i>

1299
01:01:53.790 --> 01:01:54.824
(FIRE CRACKLING)

1300
01:01:54.926 --> 01:01:57.491
<i>♪ Your skin makes me cry ♪</i>

1301
01:01:58.399 --> 01:02:00.736
(SCRAPING)

1302
01:02:03.735 --> 01:02:05.741
(GROANING. WHEEZING)

1303
01:02:12.676 --> 01:02:13.941
(SHUSHES)

1304
01:02:14.043 --> 01:02:15.678
(MOUTHING IMPERCEPTIBLY)

1305
01:02:15.780 --> 01:02:17.918
(WHIMPERING SOFTLY)

1306
01:02:19.486 --> 01:02:20.921
(MOUTHING) No.

1307
01:02:22.151 --> 01:02:23.819
(OBJECTS CLANKING IN DISTANCE)

1308
01:02:23.921 --> 01:02:26.289
<i>♪ And I'm a creep ♪</i>

1309
01:02:28.629 --> 01:02:30.091
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1310
01:02:30.193 --> 01:02:32.493
(WOMAN WHISPERING
INDISTINCTLY)

1311
01:02:38.735 --> 01:02:40.908
(PANTING)

1312
01:02:47.181 --> 01:02:50.049
- (MR. REED HUMMING)
<i>- (CREEP</i> CONTINUES PLAYING)

1313
01:02:51.253 --> 01:02:52.812
(PANTING)

1314
01:02:52.915 --> 01:02:53.882
(RATTLING)

1315
01:02:53.984 --> 01:02:55.483
<i>♪ I wanna have control ♪</i>

1316
01:02:58.924 --> 01:03:00.787
<i>♪ I want a perfect body ♪</i>

1317
01:03:00.890 --> 01:03:03.227
(SCRAPING)

1318
01:03:04.128 --> 01:03:05.829
(SCRAPING.
THUDDING BEHIND DOOR)

1319
01:03:05.931 --> 01:03:08.936
<i>♪ I want a perfect soul ♪</i>

1320
01:03:10.539 --> 01:03:13.237
<i>♪ I want you to notice ♪</i>

1321
01:03:16.105 --> 01:03:17.838
<i>♪ When I'm not around ♪</i>

1322
01:03:17.940 --> 01:03:20.310
(LOUD BANGING)

1323
01:03:21.617 --> 01:03:24.578
<i>♪ You're so very special ♪</i>

1324
01:03:27.721 --> 01:03:29.924
<i>♪ But I'm a creep ♪</i>

1325
01:03:33.693 --> 01:03:36.557
<i>♪ I'm a weirdo ♪</i>

1326
01:03:38.768 --> 01:03:42.101
<i>♪ What the hell
am I doin' here? ♪</i>

1327
01:03:44.936 --> 01:03:46.841
<i>♪ I don't belong here ♪</i>

1328
01:03:46.943 --> 01:03:48.503
- (TAPE PLAYER SCREECHES)
<i>- (CREEP</i> STOPS PLAYING)

1329
01:03:51.210 --> 01:03:52.679
MR. REED OVER SPEAKERS:
<i>I had to be sure</i>

1330
01:03:52.781 --> 01:03:54.311
<i>before I introduced you
to her.</i>

1331
01:03:55.344 --> 01:03:57.848
Sure about what?
(BREATH TREMBLING)

1332
01:03:57.950 --> 01:03:59.888
You are now in the presence

1333
01:04:00.788 --> 01:04:02.920
of a living prophet of God.

1334
01:04:03.022 --> 01:04:05.355
(WOMAN WHISPERING
INDISTINCTLY)

1335
01:04:10.997 --> 01:04:13.264
- (WOMAN WHEEZING)
- (BONES CRACKING)

1336
01:04:20.436 --> 01:04:21.842
MR. REED: <i>The reason
I invited you</i>

1337
01:04:21.944 --> 01:04:24.072
<i>into my sanctuary tonight
is because</i>

1338
01:04:24.174 --> 01:04:25.980
<i>I have been shown a miracle.</i>

1339
01:04:27.179 --> 01:04:28.542
<i>I believe
this miracle is proof</i>

1340
01:04:28.644 --> 01:04:31.478
<i>that all known religions
are demonstrably false.</i>

1341
01:04:31.581 --> 01:04:36.122
<i>and only an ancient echo
of something true.</i>

1342
01:04:37.856 --> 01:04:39.552
<i>I need a witness.</i>

1343
01:04:39.655 --> 01:04:44.097
<i>you. to verify
that the miracle is real.</i>

1344
01:04:45.931 --> 01:04:48.134
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

1345
01:04:58.674 --> 01:05:01.582
<i>Now. our family recipe
for blueberry pie is.</i>

1346
01:05:01.684 --> 01:05:03.182
<i>I think. a traditional one.</i>

1347
01:05:03.284 --> 01:05:06.419
The ingredients include
butter. flour. corn starch.

1348
01:05:06.521 --> 01:05:07.851
sugar. lemon.

1349
01:05:07.953 --> 01:05:09.824
blueberries. of course.

1350
01:05:09.927 --> 01:05:12.789
but tonight I've also included
some wolf's bane

1351
01:05:12.891 --> 01:05:14.226
and some belladonna.

1352
01:05:15.259 --> 01:05:18.461
which means that.
in a short while.

1353
01:05:20.300 --> 01:05:23.799
the Prophet will be dead
from consuming the pie.

1354
01:05:23.901 --> 01:05:26.073
(SQUELCHING)

1355
01:05:27.139 --> 01:05:28.169
MR. REED OVER SPEAKERS:
<i>Then.</i>

1356
01:05:28.271 --> 01:05:31.243
<i>you will witness a miracle.</i>

1357
01:05:32.911 --> 01:05:35.082
By the grace of God.

1358
01:05:36.553 --> 01:05:37.953
she will be resurrected.

1359
01:05:38.455 --> 01:05:40.648
(WHEEZING WEAKLY)

1360
01:05:46.322 --> 01:05:48.656
(CONTINUES WHEEZING WEAKLY)

1361
01:06:09.049 --> 01:06:11.019
- (RETCHES)
- (LANTERN CLATTERS)

1362
01:06:16.187 --> 01:06:17.652
Now. feel her pulse. please.

1363
01:06:19.088 --> 01:06:20.259
Both of you.

1364
01:06:21.596 --> 01:06:23.226
(WATER DRIPPING)

1365
01:06:23.328 --> 01:06:24.632
MR. REED OVER SPEAKERS:
<i>I need you</i>

1366
01:06:24.734 --> 01:06:27.134
<i>to feel her pulse right now!</i>

1367
01:06:31.135 --> 01:06:32.534
(PAXTON BREATHING HEAVILY)

1368
01:06:32.636 --> 01:06:34.205
MR. REED OVER SPEAKERS:
<i>Acknowledge. please.</i>

1369
01:06:34.307 --> 01:06:36.336
<i>that her heart has now
stopped pumping.</i>

1370
01:06:36.438 --> 01:06:38.672
<i>Do you know how to do that?</i>

1371
01:06:38.774 --> 01:06:40.477
<i>Index and middle finger
on the side of the neck.</i>

1372
01:06:40.579 --> 01:06:43.612
<i>in the soft. hollow area
just beside the windpipe.</i>

1373
01:06:45.247 --> 01:06:46.616
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1374
01:06:46.718 --> 01:06:49.354
MR. REED: <i>Both of you. please.
lift her head to be sure.</i>

1375
01:06:52.594 --> 01:06:54.260
(SQUELCHING)

1376
01:06:56.731 --> 01:06:59.034
(PAXTON SHUDDERS)

1377
01:07:00.871 --> 01:07:01.834
- (PROPHET GURGLES)
- (PAXTON GASPS)

1378
01:07:01.936 --> 01:07:03.236
PAXTON: She moved! She moved!

1379
01:07:03.338 --> 01:07:05.805
MR. REED: (LAUGHING) <i>That was
just a catalytic spasm.</i>

1380
01:07:05.907 --> 01:07:07.235
PAXTON: (GASPS) She's alive!

1381
01:07:07.338 --> 01:07:08.910
MR. REED: <i>No! No. no. Not yet.</i>

1382
01:07:09.012 --> 01:07:10.572
<i>Chemicals being released
into her body.</i>

1383
01:07:10.674 --> 01:07:12.546
<i>Acknowledge. please.
that there's no pulse.</i>

1384
01:07:12.648 --> 01:07:13.678
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

1385
01:07:13.780 --> 01:07:14.781
<i>Acknowledge!</i>

1386
01:07:14.883 --> 01:07:15.913
- No. No pulse.
- No pulse.

1387
01:07:16.015 --> 01:07:17.150
MR. REED: <i>Thank you.</i>

1388
01:07:17.252 --> 01:07:19.516
<i>Acknowledge that she is
no longer breathing.</i>

1389
01:07:22.054 --> 01:07:23.223
<i>Do you feel a breath?</i>

1390
01:07:27.993 --> 01:07:29.127
BARNES: No. No.

1391
01:07:29.229 --> 01:07:30.258
MR. REED: <i>So she's dead.</i>
BARNES: Yes.

1392
01:07:30.361 --> 01:07:32.133
- (WHIMPERS)
- MR. REED: <i>Okay.</i>

1393
01:07:32.733 --> 01:07:34.268
<i>Thank you.</i>

1394
01:07:34.370 --> 01:07:39.536
<i>A moment longer. and you will
witness a resurrection.</i>

1395
01:07:40.669 --> 01:07:43.271
<i>She'll return
and she will tell us</i>

1396
01:07:43.374 --> 01:07:45.212
<i>what she saw in the afterlife.</i>

1397
01:07:47.948 --> 01:07:49.249
Has the Prophet moved?

1398
01:07:49.950 --> 01:07:51.483
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1399
01:07:51.585 --> 01:07:53.084
No.

1400
01:07:53.186 --> 01:07:54.148
MR. REED OVER SPEAKERS:
<i>Hello?</i>

1401
01:07:54.250 --> 01:07:55.853
- No. No.
- Mmm-mmm.

1402
01:07:55.955 --> 01:07:57.057
(BARNES WHIMPERS)

1403
01:07:57.160 --> 01:07:59.754
MR. REED: <i>All right.
Just</i> un momentino.

1404
01:08:04.833 --> 01:08:06.233
<i>Only a moment longer.</i>

1405
01:08:07.803 --> 01:08:09.731
- (BELL RINGING)
- (GASPS)

1406
01:08:11.600 --> 01:08:13.207
(BREATHING RAPIDLY)
The Elders?

1407
01:08:15.644 --> 01:08:17.673
(DOORBELL RINGS)

1408
01:08:20.111 --> 01:08:21.977
(FOOTSTEPS ECHOING)

1409
01:08:22.079 --> 01:08:24.317
(DOOR LOCKS)

1410
01:08:28.453 --> 01:08:30.620
- (TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)
- (BOTH PANTING)

1411
01:08:33.122 --> 01:08:35.158
(PANTING)

1412
01:08:35.260 --> 01:08:37.262
- We scream.
- We scream.

1413
01:08:37.364 --> 01:08:39.728
BARNES: But not until
he answers the door.

1414
01:08:45.608 --> 01:08:47.375
(KNOCKING)

1415
01:08:48.244 --> 01:08:49.777
PAXTON: He's coming back.
BARNES: Scream! Scream!

1416
01:08:49.879 --> 01:08:51.777
(PAXTON AND BARNES SCREAMING)

1417
01:08:51.879 --> 01:08:52.673
(DOOR CREAKING)

1418
01:08:52.775 --> 01:08:55.216
- (DOOR SHUTS)
- (BOTH CONTINUE SCREAMING)

1419
01:08:55.816 --> 01:08:56.844
(LIGHTS CLICK)

1420
01:09:00.723 --> 01:09:01.882
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

1421
01:09:03.692 --> 01:09:05.019
(KNOCKING)

1422
01:09:05.121 --> 01:09:06.458
Coming!

1423
01:09:07.629 --> 01:09:09.626
(TICKING)

1424
01:09:14.967 --> 01:09:15.935
Ah! Sorry!

1425
01:09:16.037 --> 01:09:17.136
I was at the back. (CHUCKLES)

1426
01:09:17.238 --> 01:09:19.040
- No. I'm sorry to bother you.
- No.

1427
01:09:19.142 --> 01:09:20.402
I'm just in the neighborhood
looking for

1428
01:09:20.504 --> 01:09:22.508
two young ladies
from my church.

1429
01:09:22.610 --> 01:09:23.574
Oh.

1430
01:09:24.473 --> 01:09:25.678
Is everything all right?

1431
01:09:25.780 --> 01:09:27.743
(BOTH SCREAMING)

1432
01:09:28.981 --> 01:09:30.310
(BOTH PANTING)

1433
01:09:30.412 --> 01:09:32.220
They can't hear us.

1434
01:09:33.188 --> 01:09:34.384
MAN: <i>I'm sure
everything's fine.</i>

1435
01:09:34.486 --> 01:09:35.688
<i>I was just wondering
if they...</i>

1436
01:09:35.790 --> 01:09:36.755
(WIND BLOWING)

1437
01:09:36.857 --> 01:09:37.824
...stopped by.

1438
01:09:37.926 --> 01:09:38.985
No. I'm sorry to say.

1439
01:09:39.087 --> 01:09:42.957
you are the first house caller
I've had all day. so.

1440
01:09:43.593 --> 01:09:45.893
- Did you see this?
- It's locked.

1441
01:09:50.035 --> 01:09:50.999
BARNES: Help.

1442
01:09:51.101 --> 01:09:52.365
Help.

1443
01:09:52.467 --> 01:09:55.070
We can pull the rug.

1444
01:09:55.172 --> 01:09:56.104
The matches.

1445
01:09:56.206 --> 01:09:58.046
We start a fire.

1446
01:09:58.148 --> 01:09:59.308
smoke out the speaking pipe
to make sure

1447
01:09:59.410 --> 01:10:01.111
the Elder knows we're here.

1448
01:10:01.213 --> 01:10:04.118
Okay. But you did ask

1449
01:10:04.221 --> 01:10:06.482
for more information
on the church. correct?

1450
01:10:06.584 --> 01:10:08.354
Uh. this...
this is the which church?

1451
01:10:08.456 --> 01:10:09.855
The Church of Jesus Christ
of Latter-day Saints.

1452
01:10:09.957 --> 01:10:12.252
Yes. yes. yes. yes.

1453
01:10:12.354 --> 01:10:14.729
(WIND BLOWING)

1454
01:10:14.831 --> 01:10:16.258
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1455
01:10:16.360 --> 01:10:18.794
BARNES: Pull. Careful.

1456
01:10:24.206 --> 01:10:25.799
Is there some other way
I can help?

1457
01:10:25.901 --> 01:10:27.868
Do you want to use my phone.
call the police?

1458
01:10:27.970 --> 01:10:29.570
- I could get my coat...
- No. no. That's fine.

1459
01:10:29.672 --> 01:10:30.771
...and come help you
look around.

1460
01:10:30.874 --> 01:10:32.445
No. no. no. no. no.
I'm sure they're not far.

1461
01:10:33.180 --> 01:10:34.281
Uh. thank you for your time.

1462
01:10:34.383 --> 01:10:36.882
All right. well. good luck.
Yeah. I mean that.

1463
01:10:36.984 --> 01:10:38.319
- Okay.
- Uh-huh.

1464
01:10:39.051 --> 01:10:40.519
(WIND BLOWING)

1465
01:10:42.122 --> 01:10:44.325
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1466
01:10:54.170 --> 01:10:56.436
- (MUSIC STOPS PLAYING)
- (DOOR CREAKS)

1467
01:11:02.074 --> 01:11:03.138
(CREAKING)

1468
01:11:03.240 --> 01:11:05.076
(FOOTSTEPS)

1469
01:11:05.178 --> 01:11:06.745
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1470
01:11:06.847 --> 01:11:07.876
(CLICKS)

1471
01:11:09.445 --> 01:11:11.649
(WATER POURING)

1472
01:11:12.688 --> 01:11:13.479
(THUD)

1473
01:11:13.581 --> 01:11:15.150
(FURNITURE DRAGGING)

1474
01:11:15.252 --> 01:11:17.017
(FOOTSTEPS)

1475
01:11:25.229 --> 01:11:26.697
(CLICKING)

1476
01:11:27.968 --> 01:11:29.332
(SCRAPING)

1477
01:11:29.435 --> 01:11:31.768
- (FLOOR CREAKING)
- (FOOTSTEPS)

1478
01:11:41.818 --> 01:11:43.076
(MR. REED COUGHS)

1479
01:11:44.151 --> 01:11:45.782
(MR. REED CLEARS THROAT)

1480
01:11:47.449 --> 01:11:49.357
(OBJECT DRAGS)

1481
01:11:55.029 --> 01:11:56.024
(TENSE MUSIC BUILDS)

1482
01:11:56.126 --> 01:11:57.563
No.

1483
01:12:04.004 --> 01:12:05.967
(CLICKING)

1484
01:12:07.007 --> 01:12:08.739
(FOOTSTEPS)

1485
01:12:09.473 --> 01:12:11.676
(BARNES BREATHING HEAVILY)

1486
01:12:13.311 --> 01:12:14.580
(BARNES GRUNTS)

1487
01:12:16.678 --> 01:12:17.744
- (THUD)
- (DOOR CREAKS)

1488
01:12:17.846 --> 01:12:19.484
PAXTON: (WHISPERING)
He's coming!

1489
01:12:19.586 --> 01:12:21.818
- (FOOTSTEPS)
- (SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

1490
01:12:22.319 --> 01:12:24.023
(DOORBELL RINGS)

1491
01:12:24.125 --> 01:12:26.119
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1492
01:12:29.799 --> 01:12:30.893
(RATTLING)

1493
01:12:31.660 --> 01:12:34.397
Yeah? Yeah? Any luck?

1494
01:12:34.499 --> 01:12:36.569
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

1495
01:12:42.712 --> 01:12:43.708
(GASPS)

1496
01:12:45.177 --> 01:12:46.614
She moved.

1497
01:12:47.316 --> 01:12:49.010
- What do you mean?
- When we were gone.

1498
01:12:52.452 --> 01:12:54.284
No.
you're remembering it wrong.

1499
01:12:54.386 --> 01:12:55.384
She hasn't moved at all.

1500
01:12:55.486 --> 01:12:56.453
Her head is different.

1501
01:12:56.555 --> 01:12:58.886
- That's where she was!
- It's not!

1502
01:12:58.989 --> 01:13:01.556
Sister. that's not
how I remember it. Please!

1503
01:13:01.658 --> 01:13:03.992
Please. just come on! Help!

1504
01:13:04.692 --> 01:13:06.533
Hold the sleeve up.

1505
01:13:09.164 --> 01:13:13.837
I'd be remiss if I didn't
ask you one question.

1506
01:13:14.538 --> 01:13:16.642
(DRAMATIC MUSIC BUILDS)

1507
01:13:18.146 --> 01:13:19.113
(MUSIC STOPS PLAYING)

1508
01:13:19.215 --> 01:13:21.647
Have you received
this booklet?

1509
01:13:22.951 --> 01:13:24.315
I have not.

1510
01:13:24.417 --> 01:13:27.020
but I will give it a look-see.

1511
01:13:27.122 --> 01:13:29.153
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1512
01:13:29.255 --> 01:13:30.154
PAXTON: Try another.

1513
01:13:30.256 --> 01:13:31.551
BARNES: I know.

1514
01:13:31.653 --> 01:13:33.956
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1515
01:13:36.997 --> 01:13:38.425
Focus.

1516
01:13:38.527 --> 01:13:40.094
(WIND BLOWING)

1517
01:13:42.102 --> 01:13:43.999
(RATTLING)

1518
01:13:44.433 --> 01:13:45.433
Faster.

1519
01:13:45.535 --> 01:13:47.134
(MATCH IGNITES)

1520
01:13:48.010 --> 01:13:48.971
(BARNES WHIMPERS)

1521
01:13:50.145 --> 01:13:52.205
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC BUILDS)

1522
01:14:01.219 --> 01:14:02.457
(GASPS)

1523
01:14:03.355 --> 01:14:04.324
(BARNES GRUNTS)

1524
01:14:04.426 --> 01:14:06.186
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC
CONTINUES PLAYING)

1525
01:14:12.728 --> 01:14:13.966
(MUSIC STOPS PLAYING)

1526
01:14:14.068 --> 01:14:16.003
(WIND GUSTING)

1527
01:14:16.105 --> 01:14:17.098
(MATCH SCRAPING ON WALL)

1528
01:14:19.943 --> 01:14:21.173
(BARNES WHIMPERS)

1529
01:14:21.275 --> 01:14:24.011
(BARNES BREATHING HEAVILY)

1530
01:14:24.113 --> 01:14:26.173
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

1531
01:14:31.119 --> 01:14:32.084
(MATCH IGNITES)

1532
01:14:32.186 --> 01:14:34.121
- (SCREAMS)
- (GASPS)

1533
01:14:34.223 --> 01:14:36.321
- (BOTH GASPING)
- (WHEEZES)

1534
01:14:36.423 --> 01:14:39.593
- (RETCHES)
- (BOTH GASPING)

1535
01:14:41.523 --> 01:14:42.697
(RETCHES)

1536
01:14:42.799 --> 01:14:43.997
(COUGHS)

1537
01:14:44.099 --> 01:14:45.929
(PROPHET WHEEZES)

1538
01:14:47.631 --> 01:14:49.967
PROPHET: Conductor...

1539
01:14:50.369 --> 01:14:54.234
says... my... name.

1540
01:14:54.977 --> 01:14:58.073
White... clouds.

1541
01:14:58.607 --> 01:15:01.476
Not... Heaven.

1542
01:15:01.578 --> 01:15:05.179
They... unplug...

1543
01:15:05.888 --> 01:15:07.852
my brain.

1544
01:15:09.089 --> 01:15:11.526
It is...

1545
01:15:12.994 --> 01:15:13.990
not...

1546
01:15:14.490 --> 01:15:16.129
real.

1547
01:15:16.231 --> 01:15:17.231
(INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1548
01:15:17.333 --> 01:15:19.564
MR. REED:
And. thank you. Prophet.

1549
01:15:19.666 --> 01:15:21.265
We are very grateful
for your passage

1550
01:15:21.367 --> 01:15:22.869
to the other side.

1551
01:15:22.972 --> 01:15:24.067
(WHEEZING)

1552
01:15:24.169 --> 01:15:28.068
Your prophecy will be recorded
into our liturgical texts.

1553
01:15:28.170 --> 01:15:31.474
Come. You must be exhausted.
Take my arm.

1554
01:15:31.576 --> 01:15:33.581
(UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING)

1555
01:15:36.218 --> 01:15:38.179
(BARNES BREATHING HEAVILY)

1556
01:15:40.849 --> 01:15:42.021
(INDISTINCT WHISPERING)

1557
01:15:42.123 --> 01:15:44.155
(INAUDIBLE)

1558
01:15:44.257 --> 01:15:46.253
(DOOR UNLOCKS)

1559
01:15:47.029 --> 01:15:48.123
(MATCH SCRAPING)

1560
01:15:50.099 --> 01:15:51.064
(PROPHET WHIMPERS)

1561
01:15:51.166 --> 01:15:52.160
(DOOR CREAKS. SHUTS)

1562
01:15:56.665 --> 01:15:57.902
Well. now.

1563
01:15:59.708 --> 01:16:01.507
You see. this is rather
interesting because...

1564
01:16:01.609 --> 01:16:03.773
- (OBJECT CLANKS)
- (MR. REED CHUCKLES)

1565
01:16:03.875 --> 01:16:08.011
I know that one of you
has been lying

1566
01:16:09.485 --> 01:16:11.813
since you first got here.
(CHUCKLING)

1567
01:16:11.915 --> 01:16:14.047
And do you know
how I know that?

1568
01:16:14.149 --> 01:16:15.748
Excuse me. can I...
can I take that?

1569
01:16:15.850 --> 01:16:17.919
I know from the way

1570
01:16:18.021 --> 01:16:22.125
that the fire reacts
to each of you.

1571
01:16:22.227 --> 01:16:23.191
A.

1572
01:16:24.966 --> 01:16:26.226
B.

1573
01:16:26.328 --> 01:16:28.569
Yeah. One of you has
a very. very... (CHUCKLING)

1574
01:16:28.671 --> 01:16:32.572
...very big secret.
but we will know more soon.

1575
01:16:32.674 --> 01:16:34.970
There will be
before you saw a woman die

1576
01:16:35.073 --> 01:16:38.137
and come back to life.
and there will be after.

1577
01:16:38.239 --> 01:16:40.306
(BLOWS) Books will be written
about it.

1578
01:16:40.408 --> 01:16:43.783
So choose your words
very carefully when I ask.

1579
01:16:44.451 --> 01:16:45.620
what did you witness?

1580
01:16:47.686 --> 01:16:48.953
Tell me. Tell me what you saw.

1581
01:16:49.751 --> 01:16:51.223
How did she...

1582
01:16:51.325 --> 01:16:52.252
I don't know...

1583
01:16:52.354 --> 01:16:54.294
And if you didn't
see something transcendental.

1584
01:16:54.396 --> 01:16:55.457
you absolutely must tell me.

1585
01:16:55.559 --> 01:16:57.130
I don't know.

1586
01:16:57.232 --> 01:16:58.092
'Cause if I'm wrong.

1587
01:16:58.194 --> 01:16:59.634
I need to hear it.
That's why you're here.

1588
01:16:59.736 --> 01:17:01.194
It's a contrived experiment.
We are your prisoners!

1589
01:17:01.297 --> 01:17:02.902
- It doesn't make sense...
- MR. REED: Oh. pooh!

1590
01:17:03.004 --> 01:17:04.065
- We're all prisoners together.
- ...for us to have an opinion!

1591
01:17:04.167 --> 01:17:05.164
You must know by now
that any of us can leave

1592
01:17:05.266 --> 01:17:07.570
whenever we want.
but why would we want.

1593
01:17:07.672 --> 01:17:08.801
after what we've seen?

1594
01:17:08.903 --> 01:17:11.309
I saw it. I saw it.

1595
01:17:11.411 --> 01:17:12.842
I heard her describe

1596
01:17:12.944 --> 01:17:14.577
what she experienced
on the other side.

1597
01:17:14.679 --> 01:17:16.580
Great! What did you hear?

1598
01:17:16.683 --> 01:17:19.848
She said
there was a conductor.

1599
01:17:19.950 --> 01:17:22.654
- Yes. Yeah.
- Did she mean angel?

1600
01:17:22.756 --> 01:17:25.151
She had a feeling
of disassociation.

1601
01:17:25.253 --> 01:17:27.994
a feeling that something
wasn't real.

1602
01:17:28.097 --> 01:17:29.125
That's it.

1603
01:17:30.132 --> 01:17:31.094
So now you know.

1604
01:17:32.662 --> 01:17:33.661
Now. we know?

1605
01:17:33.763 --> 01:17:35.065
Yeah. now. you know.

1606
01:17:36.302 --> 01:17:37.265
Know?

1607
01:17:38.504 --> 01:17:39.872
I can show you God.

1608
01:17:41.310 --> 01:17:43.973
If you're willing to die.

1609
01:17:44.076 --> 01:17:46.942
It... it can be painless.
It can be temporary.

1610
01:17:47.044 --> 01:17:49.178
Like the Prophet.
you can be brought back.

1611
01:17:50.246 --> 01:17:51.851
It doesn't have
to be frightening at all.

1612
01:17:51.953 --> 01:17:53.386
I'll tell you... I'll tell you
what's frightening.

1613
01:17:53.488 --> 01:17:54.919
Not knowing is frightening!

1614
01:17:55.021 --> 01:17:56.552
Where do we come from?
What are we doing here?

1615
01:17:56.654 --> 01:17:57.890
What's our purpose?

1616
01:17:57.992 --> 01:18:00.791
The terror of those questions
is why religions exist.

1617
01:18:00.893 --> 01:18:02.662
I can answer
those questions for you.

1618
01:18:02.765 --> 01:18:05.964
I can give you a comfort
no religion in the world

1619
01:18:06.731 --> 01:18:08.032
is capable of giving you.

1620
01:18:10.064 --> 01:18:11.970
It all makes sense now.

1621
01:18:14.104 --> 01:18:16.205
I've been asking myself
all night.

1622
01:18:17.174 --> 01:18:19.739
how is he gonna
make killing us our idea?

1623
01:18:19.841 --> 01:18:21.012
(MR. REED SIGHS)

1624
01:18:22.948 --> 01:18:24.316
Sister Barnes.
you're in a muddle.

1625
01:18:24.418 --> 01:18:25.178
I know. I can't tell

1626
01:18:25.280 --> 01:18:27.249
if you're playing chess
or checkers.

1627
01:18:27.782 --> 01:18:29.422
Monopoly!

1628
01:18:29.524 --> 01:18:30.555
Come on. it was right there.

1629
01:18:30.657 --> 01:18:32.523
You didn't show us a miracle.

1630
01:18:32.625 --> 01:18:34.256
Okay. what did I show you?

1631
01:18:34.858 --> 01:18:36.696
That wasn't a miracle.

1632
01:18:36.798 --> 01:18:38.529
MR. REED: So you say.
What did I show you?

1633
01:18:38.631 --> 01:18:40.629
That was not a miracle!

1634
01:18:40.731 --> 01:18:42.099
What did I show you?

1635
01:18:43.834 --> 01:18:46.367
It was a magic trick.

1636
01:18:48.311 --> 01:18:49.639
MR. REED: A magic trick?

1637
01:18:49.741 --> 01:18:51.944
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1638
01:18:54.982 --> 01:18:57.980
You wanna know why
we don't talk about Taco Bell?

1639
01:18:58.082 --> 01:18:59.820
It killed me
when I was four years old.

1640
01:18:59.922 --> 01:19:03.018
Fifty people were hospitalized
from an E. coli outbreak.

1641
01:19:03.120 --> 01:19:04.985
The kids at school
called me Taco Hell

1642
01:19:05.087 --> 01:19:06.560
'cause I was clinically dead

1643
01:19:06.662 --> 01:19:08.928
while doctors operated
on my kidneys.

1644
01:19:11.365 --> 01:19:13.095
When I was dead.

1645
01:19:13.197 --> 01:19:17.068
I saw exactly
what your prophet described.

1646
01:19:17.802 --> 01:19:19.400
A blinding white light.

1647
01:19:19.502 --> 01:19:23.040
clouds. but not Heaven.
a sense of wanting to return.

1648
01:19:23.142 --> 01:19:25.813
a feeling that my state
of reality wasn't real.

1649
01:19:27.812 --> 01:19:29.410
That wasn't a prophecy.

1650
01:19:30.279 --> 01:19:33.652
That was a near-death
experience.

1651
01:19:33.754 --> 01:19:35.050
When the oxygen
leaves your brain

1652
01:19:35.152 --> 01:19:37.721
or your heart stops pumping.
your mind

1653
01:19:37.823 --> 01:19:39.593
creates unbelievable things.

1654
01:19:39.695 --> 01:19:43.094
I think you've been
keeping this woman

1655
01:19:43.196 --> 01:19:45.224
on the edge of death
in order to ask her questions

1656
01:19:45.326 --> 01:19:47.733
about meaningless
hallucinations

1657
01:19:47.835 --> 01:19:50.065
so that you can substantiate
your idea

1658
01:19:50.167 --> 01:19:53.467
of what the one.
true religion really is.

1659
01:19:54.674 --> 01:19:56.510
MR. REED: Did you know...

1660
01:19:56.612 --> 01:19:57.576
that when you remember
something.

1661
01:19:57.678 --> 01:19:58.745
you're really only remembering

1662
01:19:58.847 --> 01:20:00.507
the last time you remembered
that experience?

1663
01:20:02.312 --> 01:20:03.609
You're not actually
recalling the event.

1664
01:20:03.711 --> 01:20:07.948
So your memory of dying
at Taco Bell... (CHUCKLING)

1665
01:20:08.050 --> 01:20:09.083
...isn't really of dying.

1666
01:20:09.185 --> 01:20:11.021
it's of the memory
of the memory

1667
01:20:11.124 --> 01:20:12.692
of the memory
of the memory of the memory...

1668
01:20:12.794 --> 01:20:16.026
stop me... (CHUCKLES)
...of that event.

1669
01:20:16.128 --> 01:20:18.127
So you're remembering
a false correlation

1670
01:20:18.229 --> 01:20:19.897
with the experience
you've just witnessed.

1671
01:20:19.999 --> 01:20:24.003
But this.
this is happening right now!

1672
01:20:24.105 --> 01:20:27.135
That's why I think.
Sister Barnes. Sister Paxton.

1673
01:20:27.237 --> 01:20:29.071
that you really need
to pay attention

1674
01:20:29.173 --> 01:20:30.711
because I promise you...
(CHUCKLING)

1675
01:20:30.813 --> 01:20:32.572
...we're not talking
about a magic trick.

1676
01:20:33.845 --> 01:20:35.883
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1677
01:20:38.879 --> 01:20:39.950
No.

1678
01:20:40.052 --> 01:20:42.623
we're talking
about magic underwear...

1679
01:20:42.725 --> 01:20:44.188
- (SLASHING)
- (MUSIC STOPS PLAYING)

1680
01:20:49.861 --> 01:20:51.129
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1681
01:20:54.965 --> 01:20:57.135
(INAUDIBLE SCREAMING)

1682
01:21:04.974 --> 01:21:07.211
(IMPERCEPTIBLE)

1683
01:21:12.015 --> 01:21:14.251
(INAUDIBLE SCREAMING)

1684
01:21:27.734 --> 01:21:29.731
(SCREAMING) Help me! Help!

1685
01:21:29.833 --> 01:21:31.631
(WIND GUSTING)

1686
01:21:35.838 --> 01:21:38.077
(SOBS)

1687
01:21:39.514 --> 01:21:40.673
(INHALES SHARPLY)

1688
01:21:42.779 --> 01:21:44.083
(SIGHS)

1689
01:21:46.719 --> 01:21:47.885
(EXHALES SHAKILY)

1690
01:21:47.987 --> 01:21:49.484
MR. REED:
She'll come back to us!

1691
01:21:50.623 --> 01:21:51.926
I promise!

1692
01:21:54.257 --> 01:21:56.396
Sister Paxton.
do not be scared!

1693
01:21:56.498 --> 01:21:57.591
She will rise again.

1694
01:21:58.367 --> 01:21:59.595
Challenge him.

1695
01:21:59.697 --> 01:22:00.660
Debate.

1696
01:22:01.370 --> 01:22:02.431
Challenge him.

1697
01:22:03.571 --> 01:22:05.335
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1698
01:22:08.674 --> 01:22:10.303
(FOOTSTEPS)

1699
01:22:10.405 --> 01:22:12.540
MR. REED: Come on. now.
Sister B.

1700
01:22:13.943 --> 01:22:15.716
Wakey-wakey!

1701
01:22:15.818 --> 01:22:17.179
- (WATER DRIPPING)
- Whoa. whoa. whoa.

1702
01:22:17.281 --> 01:22:18.884
whoa. whoa. whoa!
No. that's not it.

1703
01:22:18.986 --> 01:22:21.687
That's not it.
That's a... a mucky pup.

1704
01:22:21.789 --> 01:22:22.957
Let's have that.
(CHUCKLES)

1705
01:22:26.221 --> 01:22:28.190
Moments. It'll be moments.

1706
01:22:28.292 --> 01:22:29.623
Let's have one
of your drum rolls. yeah?

1707
01:22:32.499 --> 01:22:33.462
Whoop!

1708
01:22:36.835 --> 01:22:38.973
Hey! (SNIFFLES)

1709
01:22:42.137 --> 01:22:43.641
I'm very sorry.

1710
01:22:43.743 --> 01:22:45.376
Something is wrong.

1711
01:22:45.845 --> 01:22:47.447
(UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING)

1712
01:22:47.549 --> 01:22:48.642
I'm now worried...

1713
01:22:50.684 --> 01:22:51.781
that she's not...

1714
01:22:51.883 --> 01:22:52.882
(BOX CUTTER OPENS)

1715
01:22:52.984 --> 01:22:54.219
...coming back to us.

1716
01:22:56.952 --> 01:22:57.985
Yeah.

1717
01:22:58.087 --> 01:22:59.556
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

1718
01:22:59.658 --> 01:23:00.825
Oh. yeah.

1719
01:23:00.928 --> 01:23:03.063
- (SOBS)
- MR. REED: Oh. yeah.

1720
01:23:06.499 --> 01:23:07.463
Yep.

1721
01:23:08.369 --> 01:23:09.333
Yep.

1722
01:23:09.899 --> 01:23:11.030
Yeah.

1723
01:23:11.132 --> 01:23:12.635
There it is.

1724
01:23:12.737 --> 01:23:13.967
(GRUNTS)

1725
01:23:14.069 --> 01:23:15.100
No. it isn't.

1726
01:23:15.202 --> 01:23:16.806
That was a vein.

1727
01:23:16.908 --> 01:23:18.004
(MR. REED GRUNTS)

1728
01:23:18.106 --> 01:23:19.810
(SQUELCHING)

1729
01:23:19.912 --> 01:23:22.647
A-ha! (CHUCKLES) A-ha.

1730
01:23:22.749 --> 01:23:24.645
(TENSE MUSIC BUILDS)

1731
01:23:25.949 --> 01:23:26.886
The implant.

1732
01:23:26.988 --> 01:23:29.518
This is why she can't
come back to us.

1733
01:23:30.591 --> 01:23:31.586
Take a look!

1734
01:23:32.528 --> 01:23:33.820
I'm very sorry.

1735
01:23:34.456 --> 01:23:37.658
But Sister Barnes.
she's a program.

1736
01:23:40.261 --> 01:23:42.196
She's not real.

1737
01:23:42.298 --> 01:23:44.038
Do you know what gave it away?

1738
01:23:44.506 --> 01:23:45.367
The candles.

1739
01:23:45.469 --> 01:23:48.104
What are you saying?
I don't understand.

1740
01:23:48.206 --> 01:23:50.077
No. no. I know.
I know. I know.

1741
01:23:50.710 --> 01:23:51.672
How could you?

1742
01:23:53.911 --> 01:23:55.676
(SHUDDERS)

1743
01:23:57.015 --> 01:23:59.350
Can you explain it to me?

1744
01:24:02.152 --> 01:24:05.088
Are you. Sister Paxton.

1745
01:24:05.190 --> 01:24:08.089
familiar with
the Daoist concept

1746
01:24:08.191 --> 01:24:09.992
of "The Butterfly Dream"?

1747
01:24:10.094 --> 01:24:11.692
PAXTON: A butterfly...

1748
01:24:11.794 --> 01:24:15.098
A butterfly flaps its wings
and causes a typhoon?

1749
01:24:15.200 --> 01:24:16.464
That is
"The Butterfly Effect."

1750
01:24:16.566 --> 01:24:19.065
Common mistake. No.
"The Butterfly Dream"...

1751
01:24:19.167 --> 01:24:20.468
(CLATTERING)

1752
01:24:20.570 --> 01:24:22.470
...concerns an ancient
Chinese philosopher

1753
01:24:22.572 --> 01:24:24.208
who asked himself
the following question.

1754
01:24:24.310 --> 01:24:26.505
- (OBJECT CLATTERS)
- "Was I a man dreaming

1755
01:24:26.607 --> 01:24:28.348
"I'm a butterfly.
or am I now..."

1756
01:24:28.450 --> 01:24:29.212
(THUD)

1757
01:24:29.314 --> 01:24:32.519
"...a butterfly dreaming
that I am a man?"

1758
01:24:32.621 --> 01:24:33.885
Come and sit down.

1759
01:24:33.988 --> 01:24:35.553
Come on.
(CLICKS TONGUE) Here.

1760
01:24:35.655 --> 01:24:36.651
(SIGHS)

1761
01:24:39.254 --> 01:24:41.326
(SCRAPING ON TABLE)

1762
01:24:44.533 --> 01:24:45.528
This is us.

1763
01:24:46.196 --> 01:24:47.995
You and me alone together.

1764
01:24:48.097 --> 01:24:49.301
That was Barnes.

1765
01:24:49.901 --> 01:24:51.105
Bye-bye. Barnes.

1766
01:24:51.974 --> 01:24:55.140
I have come
to a dark realization

1767
01:24:55.242 --> 01:24:58.409
that we exist inside
a simulation so advanced

1768
01:24:58.511 --> 01:25:01.280
that we cannot tell the
difference between real life

1769
01:25:02.245 --> 01:25:03.480
and artificial dream.

1770
01:25:03.582 --> 01:25:08.419
You heard the Prophet.
She said. "It is not real."

1771
01:25:08.521 --> 01:25:11.354
You see. fire dynamics
are very difficult to render.

1772
01:25:11.456 --> 01:25:14.059
I've noticed this anomaly
in its behavior

1773
01:25:14.161 --> 01:25:16.256
when it interacts
with simulated NPCs.

1774
01:25:16.358 --> 01:25:19.363
like poor old Sister B.

1775
01:25:19.465 --> 01:25:23.102
She couldn't come back to us.
but when you die.

1776
01:25:23.205 --> 01:25:28.073
finger. please.
you will pass through death

1777
01:25:28.175 --> 01:25:30.270
- and wake up...
- (BOX CUTTER RATTLES)

1778
01:25:30.372 --> 01:25:31.773
...into the real world.

1779
01:25:32.175 --> 01:25:33.646
What do you think?

1780
01:25:33.748 --> 01:25:35.149
Yes. no. maybe?

1781
01:25:36.617 --> 01:25:37.679
Um...

1782
01:25:40.589 --> 01:25:42.156
That's a theory.

1783
01:25:43.619 --> 01:25:45.390
Well yeah.
you're very welcome to...

1784
01:25:46.490 --> 01:25:48.195
to challenge my premise.
I love that.

1785
01:25:50.229 --> 01:25:51.630
- (BOX CUTTER CLOSES)
- Go for it.

1786
01:25:51.732 --> 01:25:53.563
(SNIFFLING)

1787
01:25:56.401 --> 01:25:59.536
I don't think
this is a microchip.

1788
01:26:00.268 --> 01:26:01.236
MR. REED: Oh?

1789
01:26:01.338 --> 01:26:04.310
I think it's a contraceptive.

1790
01:26:06.211 --> 01:26:09.348
A... a birth control implant.

1791
01:26:10.881 --> 01:26:11.878
Huh.

1792
01:26:13.415 --> 01:26:15.682
Tell me. have you ever met

1793
01:26:15.785 --> 01:26:18.456
a Mormon missionary
who was on birth control?

1794
01:26:20.262 --> 01:26:25.229
Did "Sister Barnes" say
she was on birth control?

1795
01:26:25.331 --> 01:26:26.832
PAXTON: Our church
would've made her

1796
01:26:26.934 --> 01:26:28.529
feel ashamed about it.

1797
01:26:28.631 --> 01:26:30.369
and she would've been
too embarrassed.

1798
01:26:31.368 --> 01:26:33.173
- Simulation theory is...
- Ah!

1799
01:26:33.275 --> 01:26:35.968
"Hypothesis." please.
Sorry. it doesn't matter.

1800
01:26:36.944 --> 01:26:39.372
Simulation hypothesis

1801
01:26:39.474 --> 01:26:42.414
is not testable. is it?

1802
01:26:43.681 --> 01:26:47.053
No. it's a matter of belief.
like any religion.

1803
01:26:47.155 --> 01:26:49.418
You either believe it.
green door.

1804
01:26:49.520 --> 01:26:51.357
or you don't believe it.
purple door.

1805
01:26:52.388 --> 01:26:54.954
With all due respect.

1806
01:26:56.190 --> 01:26:57.363
I...

1807
01:26:57.964 --> 01:26:59.829
I don't believe it.

1808
01:27:00.599 --> 01:27:04.467
I'm not smart enough
to say why. I just don't.

1809
01:27:04.570 --> 01:27:06.867
Do you believe the miracle
that I showed you?

1810
01:27:07.676 --> 01:27:08.435
PAXTON: Yes.

1811
01:27:08.537 --> 01:27:10.343
- Yeah?
- PAXTON: At first.

1812
01:27:12.042 --> 01:27:13.342
But now?

1813
01:27:13.444 --> 01:27:15.914
I think something
happened tonight

1814
01:27:16.016 --> 01:27:18.051
that you didn't expect.

1815
01:27:18.153 --> 01:27:19.746
It feels like
you're improvising.

1816
01:27:19.849 --> 01:27:22.351
trying to convince me
of a simulation theory

1817
01:27:22.453 --> 01:27:24.588
that's not sticking.
Am I right?

1818
01:27:27.494 --> 01:27:30.764
Uh. (CHUCKLES) are you
asking me if you're right

1819
01:27:30.866 --> 01:27:31.825
that I am improvising

1820
01:27:31.927 --> 01:27:35.294
or you're right
that the simulation narrative

1821
01:27:35.396 --> 01:27:36.331
is not sticking?

1822
01:27:36.434 --> 01:27:38.866
- Yes.
- (TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1823
01:27:41.677 --> 01:27:42.908
High-five.

1824
01:27:43.010 --> 01:27:45.004
(GRUNTS SOFTLY. CHUCKLES)

1825
01:27:46.248 --> 01:27:47.709
So. in fact.
you agree with your friend.

1826
01:27:47.811 --> 01:27:50.248
You think that the Prophet
was just hallucinating

1827
01:27:50.350 --> 01:27:52.484
a meaningless.
near-death experience.

1828
01:27:53.082 --> 01:27:54.212
No.

1829
01:27:54.848 --> 01:27:56.987
I think you switched
the bodies.

1830
01:27:57.089 --> 01:27:59.191
(MUSIC FADES OUT)

1831
01:27:59.293 --> 01:28:01.625
I just haven't
figured out how yet.

1832
01:28:03.424 --> 01:28:04.628
I switched...

1833
01:28:05.261 --> 01:28:06.531
the bodies?

1834
01:28:08.297 --> 01:28:09.534
(FIRE CRACKLING)

1835
01:28:11.899 --> 01:28:14.768
The doorbell rang
when the Elder got here.

1836
01:28:14.870 --> 01:28:17.804
- (TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)
- (DOORBELL RINGING)

1837
01:28:17.906 --> 01:28:19.806
<i>Which drew our attention
to the stairs.</i>

1838
01:28:19.908 --> 01:28:22.514
<i>You would have been
prepared for that.</i>

1839
01:28:25.185 --> 01:28:26.486
When we came back downstairs.

1840
01:28:26.588 --> 01:28:30.218
I noticed the woman wasn't in
the same position as before.

1841
01:28:30.320 --> 01:28:32.090
It was similar...

1842
01:28:32.193 --> 01:28:33.124
PAXTON: <i>Her head is different.</i>

1843
01:28:33.227 --> 01:28:36.396
<i>But it was not the exact same.</i>

1844
01:28:36.498 --> 01:28:40.064
<i>I think another woman
who looked exactly like her</i>

1845
01:28:40.166 --> 01:28:41.333
<i>came into the basement</i>

1846
01:28:41.435 --> 01:28:43.635
<i>through a hidden door
or something.</i>

1847
01:28:43.737 --> 01:28:47.134
disposed of her body and then
took her place at the table.

1848
01:28:47.236 --> 01:28:48.273
I see.

1849
01:28:48.375 --> 01:28:51.276
And then.
once we got back downstairs.

1850
01:28:51.378 --> 01:28:55.542
<i>she read off
a scripted prophecy</i>

1851
01:28:55.644 --> 01:28:57.747
<i>that you prepared for her.</i>

1852
01:28:58.716 --> 01:29:02.481
<i>Except the last thing
she said was.</i>

1853
01:29:02.583 --> 01:29:03.889
<i>"It is not real."</i>

1854
01:29:03.991 --> 01:29:06.521
...not... real...

1855
01:29:06.623 --> 01:29:09.259
Maybe she was trying
to tell us

1856
01:29:09.361 --> 01:29:11.761
that the miracle wasn't real.

1857
01:29:13.635 --> 01:29:14.599
Ah.

1858
01:29:15.829 --> 01:29:17.468
You see what I mean when I say

1859
01:29:17.570 --> 01:29:19.902
something happened
that you didn't expect?

1860
01:29:20.004 --> 01:29:23.340
I think you gave her a script.
and she went off the book.

1861
01:29:23.442 --> 01:29:25.071
and now you're
trying to recover.

1862
01:29:27.248 --> 01:29:29.042
Well. if that's right.
then. uh.

1863
01:29:30.310 --> 01:29:32.914
there'd have to be another way
into this basement. yeah?

1864
01:29:34.022 --> 01:29:35.048
Shall we have a look?

1865
01:29:36.222 --> 01:29:38.392
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1866
01:29:42.492 --> 01:29:43.760
I don't think there is.

1867
01:29:44.358 --> 01:29:45.796
No.

1868
01:29:46.232 --> 01:29:48.031
I'm not doing very well.

1869
01:29:48.133 --> 01:29:49.568
Sister Paxton.

1870
01:29:50.002 --> 01:29:51.771
Unless...

1871
01:29:51.873 --> 01:29:52.901
(WATER DRIPPING)

1872
01:30:01.181 --> 01:30:03.175
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1873
01:30:10.826 --> 01:30:11.788
(RATTLING)

1874
01:30:21.035 --> 01:30:22.997
(WATER POURING)

1875
01:30:23.971 --> 01:30:25.934
(WATER DRAINING)

1876
01:30:38.353 --> 01:30:40.553
- (CLANKING)
- (MUSIC STOPS PLAYING)

1877
01:30:42.517 --> 01:30:44.689
(CREAKING)

1878
01:30:51.197 --> 01:30:52.730
Which means that...

1879
01:30:54.030 --> 01:30:55.496
there would have to be
a dead body down there

1880
01:30:55.598 --> 01:30:57.232
if you were right. huh?

1881
01:30:57.334 --> 01:30:58.705
PAXTON: Correct.

1882
01:30:59.407 --> 01:31:00.804
MR. REED: How will you
test your theory?

1883
01:31:01.439 --> 01:31:02.839
(SIGHS) I don't know.

1884
01:31:03.874 --> 01:31:06.411
MR. REED: But will you go
into that hole and

1885
01:31:06.513 --> 01:31:08.111
see if there's
somebody down there?

1886
01:31:08.213 --> 01:31:09.582
If I have to.

1887
01:31:10.417 --> 01:31:11.650
MR. REED: Why would you
do that?

1888
01:31:13.420 --> 01:31:16.356
Because I want
to know the truth.

1889
01:31:16.458 --> 01:31:18.723
and because the only way out
is through.

1890
01:31:19.961 --> 01:31:20.989
Robert Frost?

1891
01:31:21.622 --> 01:31:22.826
<i>Swamp Thing.</i>

1892
01:31:23.426 --> 01:31:24.828
(CHUCKLES)

1893
01:31:26.333 --> 01:31:27.765
Don't go into that cellar...

1894
01:31:29.599 --> 01:31:31.271
unless you are prepared

1895
01:31:31.373 --> 01:31:33.270
to discover the one.
true religion.

1896
01:31:33.372 --> 01:31:35.575
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1897
01:31:44.316 --> 01:31:46.520
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

1898
01:31:47.318 --> 01:31:48.687
(SNIFFLES)

1899
01:31:50.421 --> 01:31:52.559
(LADDER CREAKS)

1900
01:32:00.267 --> 01:32:02.228
(RISING SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC)

1901
01:32:06.636 --> 01:32:08.303
- (MUSIC STOPS)
- (SIGHS)

1902
01:32:08.405 --> 01:32:10.137
(FOOTSTEPS)

1903
01:32:17.612 --> 01:32:19.052
I knew it.

1904
01:32:19.154 --> 01:32:20.818
(DOOR CREAKS AND SLAMS)

1905
01:32:25.192 --> 01:32:27.394
(HEAVY BREATHING)

1906
01:32:27.496 --> 01:32:29.662
- (WATER SPLASHING)
- (TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1907
01:32:37.304 --> 01:32:39.202
(LOCK CREAKS AND CLICKS)

1908
01:32:39.304 --> 01:32:41.135
(DOOR CREAKS)

1909
01:32:45.874 --> 01:32:48.043
(CONTINUES HEAVY BREATHING)

1910
01:32:52.814 --> 01:32:55.017
(UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING)

1911
01:33:00.325 --> 01:33:02.057
(DOOR CREAKS)

1912
01:33:13.470 --> 01:33:15.037
(SHARP INHALE)

1913
01:33:16.606 --> 01:33:18.843
(DOOR CREAKING)

1914
01:33:24.217 --> 01:33:25.982
(WATER DRIPPING)

1915
01:33:28.453 --> 01:33:30.690
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1916
01:33:38.696 --> 01:33:40.898
(CONTINUES HEAVY BREATHING)

1917
01:33:45.835 --> 01:33:48.070
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

1918
01:34:01.121 --> 01:34:02.385
(GASPS)

1919
01:34:02.487 --> 01:34:04.053
(HEAVY BREATHING)

1920
01:34:09.428 --> 01:34:11.031
(MUSIC FADES OUT)

1921
01:34:11.133 --> 01:34:13.062
(DOOR CREAKING)

1922
01:34:16.499 --> 01:34:17.434
(CLANK)

1923
01:34:17.536 --> 01:34:18.797
(DISTANT WEAK WHEEZING)

1924
01:34:18.899 --> 01:34:20.438
(SHUDDERING BREATH)

1925
01:34:20.540 --> 01:34:22.368
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

1926
01:34:32.087 --> 01:34:34.083
(COUGHING)

1927
01:34:34.617 --> 01:34:36.584
(FAINT GROANING)

1928
01:34:36.686 --> 01:34:39.055
(SHIVERING BREATH)

1929
01:34:44.097 --> 01:34:45.094
Hey.

1930
01:34:49.632 --> 01:34:50.935
(SNIFFLES)

1931
01:34:55.474 --> 01:34:56.435
(PAXTON SHIVERING)

1932
01:35:02.009 --> 01:35:03.915
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

1933
01:35:08.719 --> 01:35:10.451
Sorry about the cold.

1934
01:35:10.554 --> 01:35:11.758
(SNIFFLES)

1935
01:35:13.087 --> 01:35:14.391
Have you figured it out yet?

1936
01:35:14.493 --> 01:35:15.454
(PAXTON SNIFFLES)

1937
01:35:18.166 --> 01:35:19.359
I think so.

1938
01:35:21.369 --> 01:35:22.428
MR. REED: So what is it?

1939
01:35:23.638 --> 01:35:28.174
What is the one.
true religion. Sister P?

1940
01:35:28.276 --> 01:35:29.339
(PAXTON SHIVERING)

1941
01:35:29.441 --> 01:35:31.142
(SNIFFLING)

1942
01:35:31.244 --> 01:35:32.240
It's...

1943
01:35:35.677 --> 01:35:36.882
(INHALES)

1944
01:35:37.879 --> 01:35:39.384
(HEAVY BREATHING)

1945
01:35:39.486 --> 01:35:41.752
When we first arrived.

1946
01:35:41.854 --> 01:35:43.952
you left us alone
in your living room.

1947
01:35:44.054 --> 01:35:45.989
(DRAMATIC. SUSPENSEFUL
MUSIC PLAYING)

1948
01:35:46.091 --> 01:35:48.253
<i>We thought you were talking
to your wife.</i>

1949
01:35:48.355 --> 01:35:50.797
<i>but you were doing
something else.</i>

1950
01:35:51.594 --> 01:35:52.897
I was.

1951
01:35:52.999 --> 01:35:55.932
PAXTON: You took a key
from Sister Barnes' coat.

1952
01:35:56.035 --> 01:35:59.399
went outside to unlock
our bikes and hide them.

1953
01:36:03.912 --> 01:36:06.241
<i>I noticed your hair was wet
when you came back</i>

1954
01:36:06.343 --> 01:36:09.441
<i>with the drinks. like you were
out in the storm.</i>

1955
01:36:09.543 --> 01:36:11.351
You did this. I assume.
because you didn't want

1956
01:36:11.453 --> 01:36:12.210
the Elder to find our bikes

1957
01:36:12.312 --> 01:36:13.548
when he came back
looking for us.

1958
01:36:13.650 --> 01:36:14.786
(LATCH CLANKS)

1959
01:36:14.888 --> 01:36:16.486
But there was something else
on your mind.

1960
01:36:16.588 --> 01:36:17.590
(WATER POURING)

1961
01:36:17.692 --> 01:36:19.793
- There was.
- (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1962
01:36:21.289 --> 01:36:22.692
PAXTON: <i>You returned
the bike key</i>

1963
01:36:22.794 --> 01:36:25.031
<i>to the wrong coat pocket.</i>

1964
01:36:25.801 --> 01:36:27.728
<i>We thought this was a mistake
you made.</i>

1965
01:36:27.830 --> 01:36:29.000
(MOUTHING) Key.

1966
01:36:30.432 --> 01:36:32.367
PAXTON: (VOICE SHAKING)
But now I know it wasn't.

1967
01:36:32.469 --> 01:36:33.765
Why?

1968
01:36:33.867 --> 01:36:34.971
(INHALES)

1969
01:36:35.074 --> 01:36:38.306
You gave the bike lock
to one of your prophets.

1970
01:36:38.408 --> 01:36:41.878
instructed them to lock
the final cellar door with it.

1971
01:36:41.980 --> 01:36:45.049
But why. why. why?
Why did I do that?

1972
01:36:45.949 --> 01:36:47.885
Because you wanted me to know

1973
01:36:47.988 --> 01:36:50.851
the only reason
I'm standing here right now

1974
01:36:50.953 --> 01:36:52.690
is because it is exactly

1975
01:36:52.792 --> 01:36:54.960
where you want me
to be standing.

1976
01:36:55.862 --> 01:36:58.093
I'm not here
because I chose to be.

1977
01:36:58.195 --> 01:37:00.527
I'm here because you made me
choose to be.

1978
01:37:00.629 --> 01:37:01.968
Oh.

1979
01:37:02.070 --> 01:37:06.402
Because you want me to believe
the one. true religion is...

1980
01:37:06.504 --> 01:37:08.306
(SIGHS)

1981
01:37:08.408 --> 01:37:09.601
...control.

1982
01:37:13.677 --> 01:37:15.447
(CHUCKLES)

1983
01:37:15.549 --> 01:37:17.147
That is exactly right.

1984
01:37:19.413 --> 01:37:22.581
Religion is just
a system of control...

1985
01:37:23.291 --> 01:37:24.886
(WHEEZING)

1986
01:37:24.988 --> 01:37:26.720
(HEAVY BREATHING)
It's okay.

1987
01:37:26.822 --> 01:37:28.059
I'll help you.

1988
01:37:28.161 --> 01:37:29.395
MR. REED: No. you see.
that's what's so interesting.

1989
01:37:29.497 --> 01:37:31.290
They don't want your help.

1990
01:37:31.392 --> 01:37:33.399
They... (CHUCKLING)
they are exactly

1991
01:37:33.501 --> 01:37:34.565
where they chose to be.

1992
01:37:34.667 --> 01:37:36.028
But you killed that woman.

1993
01:37:36.130 --> 01:37:37.230
MR. REED: I disagree.

1994
01:37:37.332 --> 01:37:39.769
She... She chose to eat
a poisoned pie

1995
01:37:39.871 --> 01:37:41.806
because of her profound faith.

1996
01:37:41.908 --> 01:37:45.707
It is called drinking the...
anyone?

1997
01:37:45.809 --> 01:37:47.542
(SNAPPING SHEARS)

1998
01:37:47.644 --> 01:37:48.841
Kool-Aid.

1999
01:37:48.943 --> 01:37:50.375
It is true...

2000
